```ts title="webhooks.ts" {2-3|5-8} lineNumbers /verify/ /drop.delivered/
app.post('/hooks', async (req, res) => {
  const signature = req.header('wren-signature');
  if (!wren.webhooks.verify(req.body, signature)) return res.sendStatus(401);

  const event = JSON.parse(req.body);
  if (event.type === 'drop.delivered') {
    await orders.markDelivered(event.drop.reference);
  }
  res.sendStatus(200);
});
```

<Notes>
`code` with a fenced block, `lineNumbers`, marked words and two highlight steps, on inverse and without an aside, so the code takes the full width; use it when a reader should find the same words in their own code later.
This is Pantry Lane's whole webhook handler. [click] First it verifies the signature, so nobody else can tell their shop a parcel arrived. [click] Then it reads the event: when a drop is delivered, it marks their own order as delivered, by their own order number. The answer is 200, and we stop retrying.
</Notes>

